  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Cut the pak choy into thirds, keeping the leaves and stems separate. Crush or finely chop the garlic. Thinly slice the tofu. Bring a medium saucepan of water to the boil for the noodles.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2248924/photos/large/prep_ingredients-5e7f56353234f413acfff1f22a8e9c2f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer soup: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Add the garlic and curry powder and cook, stirring, for 1 min or until fragrant. Add the coconut milk and 375ml (1½ cups) water and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to medium and cook, stirring occasionally, for 8 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2248925/photos/large/brown_chicken-ca90ec08e97bbbfc7bc83c00e6cb8144.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook noodles: Meanwhile, add the noodles to the pan of boiling water and cook for 7 mins or until tender. Drain, then rinse under hot water to prevent the noodles from sticking.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2248926/photos/large/simmer_laksa-b3b01de1515d47ac06b52dd1c492338e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add tofu to soup: Add the tofu and pak choy stems to the soup and cook for 3 mins or until the pak choy is tender and the tofu is warmed through. Add the pak choy leaves and cook for a further 1 min or until wilted.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2248927/photos/large/cook_noodles-da9132540e9bce376ec61936fb5f1930.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Stir 2 tsp white vinegar and 2 tsp soy sauce into the soup. Taste, then season with pepper. Divide the noodles among bowls and spoon over the soup. Scatter over the fried shallots and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2248928/photos/large/serve_up-31fed263f380ff273a18f3cc0d4d5cfa.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it spicy: If you like a kick of heat, scatter over a pinch of chilli flakes or thinly sliced fresh chilli just before serving.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2248929/photos/large/make_it_yours-d97c1e264e0a6f2fdab7550eed5c4dce.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
